 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "how-to",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300,
   "w": 520,
   "page": "page-1",
   "text": "Click through the app: For You \u2192 a card \u2192 Fire \u2192 Simulate completion. Sidebar switches Notes / Graph / Excluded / Settings. The tweak chips above each frame jump to any screen or flip dark mode.\n\nFirst-time tips are on in this prototype: each plays once and disappears when you do what it asks. Settings \u2192 About \u2192 Replay brings them back."
  },
  {
   "id": "hands-note",
   "x": 1560,
   "y": 1300,
   "w": 420,
   "page": "page-1",
   "text": "Hands is triggered by holding right \u2318 on a real Mac; the pills at the bottom-left of the frame simulate that here."
  },
  {
   "id": "board-note",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300,
   "w": 520,
   "page": "page-2",
   "text": "Every screen, in flow order, with first-time tips off. Names, people and numbers are sample data."
  },
  {
   "id": "ftue-note",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300,
   "w": 560,
   "page": "page-3",
   "text": "One tip per screen, keyed: foryou \u00b7 card \u00b7 knowledge \u00b7 graph \u00b7 excluded \u00b7 sources \u00b7 hands. The target is spotlit, the rest dims. The tip completes only when the user performs the action (Skip also counts), is stored on disk, and never returns unless replayed from Settings \u2192 About."
  }
